        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0806" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 195.1/43</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil </hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-14T18:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 14, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Robert Dollar</hi> was given provisional
                    certificate of registration as American vessel several days since by American
                    Consul <pb facs="0807" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/> General, Rio de Janiero, under
                    instructions transmitted by this Department showing that vessel had regularly
                    been transferred to American ownership and entitled to American registration
                    under laws of United States. Reported that vessel denied clearance by Brazilian
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>Investigate and request release and clearance of vessel, that it may proceed at
                    once to American port.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
